\f0\fs24 \cf0 Chanta approached loading dock 20, located at the rear of Hardy Tower 1, but prior to entry he made one last glance around to ensure he had not been followed. He entered the dock and approached a non-descript lightly painted brick wall that, upon his approach, began to shimmer before revealing itself as an elevator door which automatically opened. As the door slid open Chanta was picked and hurled into the elevator by two darkly dressed and serious looking dudes. 
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Hey! What the fuck fellas?\'94 Chanta queried. 
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Shut the fuck up little man.\'94 The taller of the two said. \'91What floor are we headed for?\'94 
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Top floor, but the controls will not work for you.\'94 Chanta replied. \'93Let me do it.\'94 Chanta rose to his feet and waived his hand in the general direction of what appeared to be a control panel and the elevator immediately shot skyward for the 210 floor trip to his penthouse. He was then struck on the back of the head and stumbled forward. \'93Ouch! What was that for, mate? I may be drunk but I am still feelin\'92 pain.\'94 
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Yeah, bullshit.\'94 Said the shorter but quite obviously stronger man who then delivered a punch that would have sent any heavyweight over the ropes to land unconscious in the third row. The blow barely knocked Chanta backwards more than a few steps. Unperturbed another blow of equal might landed on Chanta\'92s nose, causing little damage and no bleeding.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Ouch! Dude, Dude\'85It\'92s not going to work.\'94 Chanta said softly, raising both hands. \'93Let\'92s just go upstairs and have a beer, you know, like civilized men.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93We have our orders.\'94 Said the strongman.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Well, let\'92s see if we can accommodate them, huh?\'94 Chanta smiled back as the two men exchanged perplexed glances. \'93If you are going to try and kill me, I\'92ve been killed before. Live on the link.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Was that you?\'94 The tall one smiled. \'93How did you survive?\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Long story, but I can assure you, those PPP\'92s you have under your jackets will do you no good.\'94 Chanta replied. \'93I\'92ve been tortured by one of the best in the business and he failed to get me to talk. So, boys, I am happy to discuss anything you want, but try and coerce me and I you will get nothing.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
The elevator door slid open revealing the luxuriant squatters apartment Chanta had claimed as his own. The darkly dressed mercinaries were simply gob-smacked by the decadence of the atrium.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Welcome to my humble abode, gentlemen.\'94 Chanta laughed and knew from their faces they had never seen anything like the opulence laid out before them. \'93So then, what do you fuckers want?\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93We know that this was the site where the massive cyber-attack on the financial system was launched.\'94 Tall guy said. 
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93What are you the fuckin\'92 police or something?\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93No, we are representing private interests.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Sounds like someone wants in on the action.\'94 Chanta countered.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93More like our client wants to protect the finance system from the likes of you. The attack has caused untold anguish to many prominent citizens\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Their anguish is nothing compared to the pain those arseholes have caused, just by their existence.\'94 Chanta said. A fist again struck his face with tremendous force and a loud smack. \'93Stop it! That fuckin\'92 hurts. I was not the author of the attack, I don\'92t know how the system work.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Who knows?\'94 The tall guy seemed to be in charge.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93I will have to make a call. Is that okay?\'94 Chanta hoped it would be.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Yes, but put it on speaker and if you say anything to give us away, I \'91ll do my very best to tear your fucking head off and we\'92ll see if you can survive that.\'94 
\f1 \

\f0 \
Chanta pulled out his hand device and made the call.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Chanta, do you know what time it is?\'94 Sarah said. \'93Voice only? Why no vid?\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93I\'92m on the shitter.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Thanks for that.\'94 Sarah sighed. \'93What\'92s so urgent?\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Look, I was in the control centre earlier and I think there is something wrong with the data base.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93How so?\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93It\'92s beeping constantly\'94 Chanta lied. \'93It sounds like an alarm and I thought it might have something to do with the last time we used the system. You know.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Yes, that does sound a little odd, but I can\'92t leave at the moment. My boy is sleeping.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Yes, Jonesy needs his sleep, but I really think this needs your immediate attention.\'94 Chanta replied. 
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93You sound strange. Are you drunk?\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Yeah, a little, but I am sobering up fast.\'94 
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93You should not be messing with that system when you have been drinking.\'94 Sarah warned. \'93I can come over in the morning.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Okay, can you tell me how it works? I am going to have a look at it myself.\'94 Chanta said.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93No, you mustn\'92t.\'94 Sarah said, concern creeping into her voice. \'93Okay, I will be there as soon as I can arrange a shuttle. Three quarters of an hour?\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Sounds good.\'94 Chanta said. \'93Don\'92t bring little Jonesy with you.\'94 He terminated the call before she could answer.
\f1 \

\f0 \
