\'93Jonesy?\'94 Sarah had no idea what Chanta meant. It was now 5.30am and upon dressing she went to the kitchen and saw Shakti at the dining table making preparations for his big day. His first big arrest.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93It looks like there\'92s even more to do after an arrest.\'94 Shakti said. \'93Who would have thought?\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93I have to go to the business district for a quick meeting with Chanta.\'94 Sarah announced.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93This early? It must be important.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93I don\'92t know, actually.\'94 Sarah replied. \'93He called Richard, Jonesy. Very odd.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93What, like that murdering Agent friend of yours?\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93He was never a friend! He tortured Chanta.\'94 Sarah shot back. \'93\'85he tortured Chanta\'85.\'94 She grabbed her palm device from her pocket and had the Head of Elvi Security on the screen in seconds. \'93Get a team together.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
Richard appeared from his bedroom and upon seeing his mother raised his hands, demanding to be picked up. Dutifully, Sarah obliged and wedged him on her right hip.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Good morning my little genius. Mummy is going on an errand today and you will have to stay at home.\'94 Sarah explained. \'93It might be dangerous.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
Richard grabbed on tight and would not let go and then he began to cry. And cry. He bellowed even louder when Shakti tried, once only, to dislodge him. He would not budge.
\f1 \

\f0 \
