\cf0 The elevator raced toward the Penthouse, Richard happily on the floor, front and centre of the elevator. He resisted his mother and any Elvi that attempted to raise him off the ground. Sarah could feel he actually wanted to be the first out of the elevator and when she made attempts to pick him up he would scream, killing any chance of a stealthy entry into the penthouse atrium.As the elevator approached its destination the rate of ascent slowed considerably. The Elvi Security Team did a final weapons check and attempted to step forward when Richard stiffened both arms and raised them sideways to the horizontal with his palms backwards. Sarah and each member of the team were frozen in place.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Richard.\'94 Sarah whispered. \'93Please, darling.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93It will be alright, mother.\'94 Richard said. 
\f1 \

\f0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'93I\'92m begging you, please.\'94 Sarah breathlessly pleaded, tears coursing out of the corner of each eye. When the shock of his first words began to sink in, Sarah did not know what was more surprising, the fact that Richard could speak perfectly well or that he spoke in a regal English accent. 
\f1 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \
As the doors slid open, Sarah\'92s mind was wild with desperate thoughts of protecting her young boy. There could, very well be nothing untoward awaiting them, but her good sense told her something else. 
\f1 \

\f0 \
Chanta stood three or four decent strides in front of the elevator and stiffened with genuine surprise when Richard stepped off the elevator alone. He could see Sarah and the security team standing mute and motionless at the back of the car and could not fathom why.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Jonesy?\'94 Chanta managed to spit out.
\f1 \

\f0 \
Richard smiled brightly and ran towards Chanta, but stopped short and turned around to see two goons standing either side of the elevator door pointing their PPP\'92s directly at him. 
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93There is a hole in your shoe.\'94 Richard said politely and then turned to Chanta, arms raised. The two gunman shrugged shoulders and shot each other in the foot.
\f1 \

\f0 \
 \'93You can speak?\'94 Chanta held him tight as he saw Sarah and the security detail pour out of the elevator and secure the two men writhing on the floor, each grasping a slippery red shoe.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Yes, Great Teacher.\'94 Richard said with a wry smile. \'93May I call you Great Teacher? I think Chanta Hardy is a little too childish for a grown man. Don\'92t you think?\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Whatever you say little buddy.\'94 Chanta was filled with joy and wondered, momentarily, what having a child of his own might be like. Nah, I\'92d fuck it up. His train of thought was disrupted by Sarah reefing Richard out of his arms and hugging him tightly. She began to sob loudly.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Don\'92t you ever do that to me again.\'94 Sarah she wailed. \'93Do you hear me? You are more important than anyone. That includes me and in definitely includes Chanta!\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Mother, dear. I love you and The Great Teacher, but I did not do this for either of you.\'94 Richard said. \'93I did it for them.\'94 He pointed to two Elvi restraining one of the prisoners. \'93They would have been shot in the head as soon as they stepped off the elevator. They were expecting a woman to step off out and as soon as they saw two men they would have opened fire. They, of course would have been killed by the rest of our team and I could not allow that either.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Who cares about those criminals?\'94 Sarah asked, her sobs dying down.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93I do. People, like species, should be allowed to evolve and this experience will give them much to reflect upon.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93How did you know what would happen?\'94 Sarah inquired.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93I saw it happen.\'94 Richard said with a degree of certainty the great sage Kleo would have deemed hubris. \'93I can\'92t explain it to you right now, but time is more flexible than you think. What we should do is find out who sent these men here.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Are you trying to take over?\'94 Sarah said jabbing him lightly in the chest. \'93Yes you are. Aren\'92t you? You are so cute. She cuddled him close, her face beaming. \'93Team Leader? Interrogate those men and find out who sent them.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Mother dear, stop that.\'94 Richard began squirming. \'93Mother, put me down. Please.\'94 Sarah place him down and he scurried off towards the interrogation. 
\f1 \

\f0 \
 \'93So cute.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93When did he start to talk?\'94 Chanta asked.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93He just started in the elevator.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Precocious little fucker.\'94 Chanta laughed. \'93Just look at him.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
Richard approached the Elvi who all bowed reverently. \'93May I speak to them, team leader?\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Of course Great One\'94 The team leader said. \'93We are here to serve.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93You chaps look a little unhappy.\'94 Richard turned to the team leader. \'93Those shoes don\'92t match, do they?\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93What? What are you crapping on about kid?\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Well, your shoes don\'92t match and it is offending my sense of symmetry. I was wondering if you would like a hole in the other shoe, that\'92s all.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93No!\'94 The prisoner cried. 
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Well then, why don\'92t you tell us who hired you.\'94 The little man smiled.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93We will be killed.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93They will probably kill you anyway, but if you help us, you will be protected.\'94 Richard pointed out.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Our client is more powerful that you can imagine.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93I am personally protected by the Elvi Nation with the backing of my grandmother, Eloise Shakti.\'94 
\f1 \

\f0 \
Both prisoners burst into laughter and could not stop. Richard was a little shaken, they laughed at the might of the Elvi, armed with the latest firepower. 
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Okay, What\'92s so funny?\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93You\'92re protected by Eloise Shakti?\'94 The second prisoner continued to cackle. \'93She\'92s our client!\'94 The prisoners writhed on the floor giggling, until the gunshot wounds stopped them.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Mother?\'94 Richard called out. \'93Mother, I think we have a problem.\'94
