\f0\b0 \cf0 \'93It is good to see new board members taking up their positions. New blood and new ideas will be needed for the challenges ahead.\'94 The CEO said, opening the annual board meeting. \'93As you know there has been a schism, for want of a better word, in the finance system which has caused a temporary reduction in expected revenue.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Yes, Mr CEO, some of our most prominent citizens are bankrupt.\'94 Eloise Shakti teased. \'93How have your fared in these hard times?\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93My portfolios is intact.\'94 The CEO lied, precipitating muted, bemused laughter from the board members. 
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93This schism, as you call it, was a deliberate attack upon the finances of the top 1% of the Dominion.\'94 Eloise said. \'93I have had my forensic accountants looking at it for weeks. The Elvi Nation\'92s investments and holding improved by 500% in a few hours. I was lucky enough to have some investments with them, along with a few of our colleagues here. Without these investments, I would be bankrupt, just like you Mr CEO.\'94 A few surprised looks and cries of shock rumbled around the giant conference table, however there were a few who were not surprised and sat, knowingly, in stoney silence.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93How dare you?\'94 The CEO stood to his feet and stared down Eloise. \'93That is an outrageous allegation. Where is your proof? I don\'92t care who you think you are, but you will not survive this meeting unless you have proof.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Every member of this board is aware your debts have been called in, you have taken out bridging finance with all sorts of predatory lenders. You are drowning in debt and I, as a member of the Board of Directors of the Primary Trade Dominion, are demanding you prove your liquidity or you will be removed from the board.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93I do not answer to you\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93You answer to the board.\'94 Eloise looked to her Boardroom Colleagues who were all nodding in agreement. 
\f1 \

\f0 \
At moment the giant double doors of the board room creaked opened, revealing the Commissioner of Police, Hayley Lanning and Lieutenant Shakti awaiting entry.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93What is this?\'94 The CEO roared. \'93Commissioner you have no business here.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Yes she does.\'94 Lieutenant Shakti stepped forward, into the room, and took a direct line to the CEO and trunig his head his head to Hayley Lanning. \'93Now?\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Not yet.\'94 Hayley rolled her eyes.
\f1 \

\f0 \
THIS IS WHERE ELOISE INTRODUCES DAMIEN HARDMAN AND TELLS THEN HE IS HER OPERATIVE.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Ichabod Carmichael Wallington-Smythe. You are under arrest for the murder of Director XXXX of the Department of Pre-emptive Reciprocity and Pro-active Euthanasia. You are not obliged to say anything unless you wish, as anything you say will be recorded and may be used in evidence. Do you understand that?\'94\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \

\f0 \'93The only thing I understand is that I am looking at two ex-police officers. I am immune from prosecution.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Cue the holo-vid.\'94 Eloise called out. \'93Let\'92s see how long that immunity lasts.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93You are in on this?\'94 The CEO asked Eloise. 
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93We are all here to see your demise\'94 said Eloise as a holo-vid hovered above the boardroom table. The CEO\'92s culpability in the death of Director XXXXXX was bared for all to see. There was no doubt he arranged the killing and in the ordinary course of events that would not have been enough to dislodge him from the CEO\'92s chair, but his weakened financial position undermined any thoughts of redemption. It was perfectly okay for him to be a murderer, most of the members of the board had ordered a killing or two in their time, but a bankrupt murderer? That was a bridge too far.
\f1 \

\f0 \
Eloise stood and looked around at her shocked colleagues, \'93Did you seek the authority of the board of directors before terminating Director\'85\'85\'85.. Contract?\'94 
\f1 \

\f0 \
The CEO stared here down but, wheezed out a feeble \'93No\'94.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Then you have breached your contract and your immunity does not extend to acts in breach of contract.\'94 Eloise took a quick look at each of member of the board. \'93I move that Ichabod Charmichael Wallington-Smythe, be removed as CEO. Do I have a second?\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93I second that\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \'93I second that\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \'93So do I\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \'93I call for a vote. A two-third\'92s majority will suffice.\'94 Eloise announced. \'93A show of hands?\'94 Immediately the right hand of every board member shot into the air. \'93Unanimous. Mr CEO, you are hereby terminated.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 \
Lieutenant Shakti and Commissioner Hayley Lanning took the CEO into custody and escorted him out of the room in silence.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Was that your son?\'94 said one of the newly minted board members.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\'93Shut up.\'94 Eloise replied. \'93The next item on the agenda is the election of a new CEO.\'94
\f1 \

